==English==
[[Image:Hoookah.jpg|thumb|right|200 px|A hookah.]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ur}} {{attention|ur|transliteration needed}} {{term|حقہ|lang=ur|sc=ur-Arab}}, from {{etyl|ar}} {{term|حقة||pot, jar|lang=ar|tr=ħúqqa}}, from {{term|حق||cavity, hollow|lang=ar|tr=ħuqq}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# a [[pipe]] with a long flexible tube that draws the [[smoke]] through [[water]]. Originally invented in India, it gained most popularity in the Arab world. It is traditionally used for smoking tobacco, which is often flavored.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|pipe with a long flexible tube}} [[hubble-bubble]], [[hubbly]], [[hubbly-bubbly]], [[hubbly bubbly]], [[narghile]], [[nargila]], [[sheesha]], [[shisha]]

